{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "expand-multifuel-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.44: the `expand-multifuel` run computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE through `moves-onroad.esm`. Its RunSpec selects four fuels for the passenger car -- gasoline, diesel, CNG and electricity -- where every other passenger-car run in this tree selects gasoline alone. MOVES expands either selection before writing `runspecsourcefueltype`, which is the table the model reads: gasoline alone became gasoline, diesel, E85 and electricity, and these four become those four and CNG.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES, which §23 asks for before a dimension is called covered, and the honest answer is: one row of one table, and none of the numbers.\n\n* A SELECTED SOURCE-FUEL PAIR WITH NO VEHICLES. `runspecsourcefueltype` is 5 rows here, (21, 1), (21, 2), (21, 3), (21, 5) and (21, 9), against 4 in `expand-day`. The default `sampleVehiclePopulation` has no passenger car on CNG at any model year, so the fifth candidate in the cohort grid finds no `svp` row and emits nothing. It is the first run in the tree whose `runspecsourcefueltype` names a pair with no population (every other one's pairs all have rows, checked over the twenty-nine), so a cohort grid that ranked its fuels by selection rather than by surviving cohort, or that emitted a zero row for a selected fuel, passed the whole suite until now.\n\n* NOTHING ELSE. `MOVESOutput` is 125 rows of running-exhaust Total Energy, fuelTypeID 1, 2, 5 and 9 -- the same 125 keys as `expand-day`'s weekday block and `process-tirewear`'s 91-01 block, and EQUAL to both at every cell (compared from the three oracles as floats, max relative difference 0). Start exhaust (9102) is selected and discarded on road type 4 as in `expand-day`. So this is a regression on the empty candidate and not a test of anything fuel-specific; a CNG passenger car would need a source type with CNG population (the transit bus, 42) or an input database.\n\nTHE THIRTEEN SELECTIONS, ONE BINDING AND THE ORACLE are everything this document carries: `runspecs/expand-day.esm` with its sources pointed at this snapshot. `n_outputRate` is 125, one emitted block.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "expand-multifuel"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
